{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>According to his wickedness, in number.</b> The letter bet is pointed with sheva, and סמך (samekh) attached to it means forty — that is, במספר (in number) forty; yet not forty literally, but the number adjacent to forty, which is thirty-nine. If so, when it says 'in number forty,' it is as if it said thirty-nine. And the reason for this number of thirty-nine for lashes is that the dead one needs revival, and this sinner who transgressed the commandments of his Master incurred the death penalty and the punishment of karet fell upon his soul; for through this [the lashes] he shall live, and the dew of revival shall return to him — to those very lives for which the soul is destined. This is what they said in tractate Megillah: all those liable to karet who received lashes are absolved from their karet. They thereby explained to us that the thirty-nine lashes are an atonement for karet, and the dew of revival returns to him, for his soul is purified and returns to its root. And there is another reason: for the liability of lashes in a court below is only from the age of thirteen years and upward, and the blows are tripled — three times thirteen is ט״ל (thirty-nine); and likewise the lashes in the court above are only from the age of twenty and upward, therefore it is sixty — three times twenty is sixty, and this is what is said: 'they brought Elijah and struck him sixty lashes of fire.' And what the Rabbis, of blessed memory, everywhere call 'forty lashes,' when they are only thirty-nine — and they did not say 'forty lacking one' as they said concerning Shabbat: 'the Fathers of labors are forty lacking one' — they followed the language of the verse, which says ארבעים יכנו, even though the word במספר adjacent to ארבעים teaches that the intent of the verse is not forty literally. And the sense of כדי רשעתו is that they administer the blows, greater or lesser, according to his wickedness, and all of them within the number forty."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:59.669583Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}